# But there's another important thing missing

If this were a **real production-quality Caregence pipeline**, I'd expect you to think about:

### Backup

Before deployment:

```text
Current application
       ↓
Backup
       ↓
New deployment
```

Because if deployment fails:

```text
New deployment
      ↓
Failure
      ↓
Rollback
```

So eventually your flow should become:

```text
Checkout
 ↓
Setup Python
 ↓
Install dependencies
 ↓
Tests
 ↓
Build/prepare
 ↓
Backup current deployment
 ↓
Deploy
 ↓
Restart Supervisor
 ↓
Check Supervisor status
 ↓
Health check
 ↓
SUCCESS
```

If health check fails:

```text
Health check ❌
      ↓
Rollback
      ↓
Restart Supervisor
      ↓
Health check again
```

